# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Champollion — .gitignore
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ONE REPO. This monorepo is the single source; distribution happens via
# npm / PyPI / the website build, not repo mirrors.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Agent configuration (local to this machine) ───────────────────
.gemini/

# ── Secrets — NEVER commit ──────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.local
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
credentials.json

# ── Research vault — internal, never published ──────────────────────
# Early-stage research and landscape analysis. Local-only from the
# public flip onward (untrack with: git rm -r --cached .vault).
.vault/

# ── OS & editor artifacts ───────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# ── Build artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.docusaurus/
build/
dist/
*.tgz
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# ── Local-only loose files (generated/downloaded, not checked in) ──
*.pdf
automata.svg
dfa.svg
ast.svg
arxiv_results.xml

# Harness run artifacts — cache batches + queue run/report logs (the reports
# embed source/expected translation pairs). Generated per-run, never committed.
/eval/

# Downloaded third-party reference papers (ACL 2026 dossier reading set) —
# bulk copyrighted content fetched on demand, never committed (see docs/ACL_2026_DOSSIER.md)
references/Research Papers/Published paper/

# Photographed ACL 2026 conference slides (IMG_*.JPG, ~81 MB) — third-party
# copyrighted presentation content, local-only, never committed
/ACL 2026 BPE slides/

# ── Data infrastructure (large/generated, never commit) ──────────
# SQLite databases — ingestion layer only, never enters any repo
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db.pre-*

# CLDF research data — 4.6 GB of linguistic datasets. Two files are
# force-tracked THROUGH this ignore (tracked files override it):
#   cli/data/cldr-supplemental/SNAPSHOT.json        (provenance pin)
#   cli/data/cldr-supplemental/scriptMetadata.json  (61 KB, Unicode-licensed;
#     the card adapters derive text direction from it — without it the
#     public repo silently loses `dir` on every card. Found 2026-08-27.)
cli/data/

# Generated trading card data — now served from Supabase
cli/website/data/tc-index.json
cli/website/data/tc-lang/
cli/website/data/languages.json
# Split /languages browsing dataset (distilled from languages.json at build)
cli/website/data/lang-index.json
cli/website/data/lang-cards/
# Homepage endonym datasets — distilled from languages.json by the shared-data
# plugin at start/build time (from cards locally, from Supabase on cold builds).
cli/website/data/channel.json
cli/website/data/wall.json
# Homepage viz — built from the Supabase scoreboard at start/build time
# (field.json + graph.json from the DB; tc-index ensured by `ensure-tc-index`).
# Build artifacts, not committed snapshots (founder directive 2026-06-16).
cli/website/data/field.json
cli/website/data/graph.json
cli/website/src/data/graph-poster.json
# Public Index ("the Catalogue") — distilled at build by the shared-data plugin
# (generateCatalogueJson.js) from the in-repo SSOTs (corpora registry, resolved
# language cards, method-registry, human-services, external-results). Generated,
# never committed; the SSOTs are the source of truth.
cli/website/data/catalogue.json
cli/website/data/catalogue-langs.json
# Localized glossary artifacts — merged at build by the shared-data plugin
# (mergeGlossaryLocale.js) from i18n/<locale>/glossary.json over the English
# SSOT. Generated, never committed; the SSOT + translated i18n files are the
# sources of truth. (Pattern does NOT match the tracked English glossary.json.)
cli/website/data/explainers/glossary.*.json

# Network artifacts — produced at build by scripts/ensure-network-artifacts.mjs
# (generate_sweep_queue.py / canonical registry copy / Supabase Storage), never
# committed. Supabase is the SSOT; these are generated/served, not source. The
# slim queue-preview.json (which the website pages fetch) STAYS committed as a
# safe build-time fallback. See cli/website/scripts/ensure-network-artifacts.mjs
# and mt-eval-arena/supabase/functions/regenerate-queue/README.md.
cli/website/static/queue.json
cli/website/static/mesh.json
cli/website/static/registry.json

# Generated Glottolog hierarchy — rebuilt on demand from cli/data/glottolog/
# by cli/scripts/build-language-tree.mjs; consumed only by data-pipeline scripts.
cli/shared/language-cards/language-tree.json

# mt-eval-arena staging data — intermediate build output
mt-eval-arena/data/


# ── crk-translate: extracted to its own repository (2026-06-22) ──────
# The Plains Cree (nêhiyawêwin) pipeline was moved OUT of this monorepo into
# the standalone repo ../champollion-crk-translate. It is no longer tracked or
# hosted here — local or remote. This blanket ignore is belt-and-suspenders so
# a stray working-tree copy can never be re-added. (The more specific
# crk-translate/eval/* content lines below are now subsumed by this rule.)
/crk-translate/

# ── EdTeKLA-derived corpora: fetch-from-source, never hosted ──────
# Champollion does not host third-party corpora. The EdTeKLA Cree
# Language Textbook data (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, University of Alberta) is
# rebuilt deterministically at run time from
# https://github.com/EdTeKLA/IndigenousLanguages_Corpora by
# corpora_builder.adapters.edtekla_adapter — config SSOT is the
# corpora card (cli/shared/corpora-cards/eval-eng-crk-edtekla-*.json,
# `source` block: repo_url/ref/builder/sha256). The harness fetches
# missing corpora into arena/datasets/.cache/ on demand (mt-eval run
# --yes accepts the license non-interactively). Working-tree copies
# of these files may exist locally but must stay untracked.
arena/datasets/.cache/
arena/datasets/crk/*.json
arena/datasets/curated/eng-crk-dev-v1.json
crk-translate/eval/textbook_gold_standard.json
# master_corpus.json additionally re-exposes sealed gold_standard and
# phase1 segments — custody is local-only (see registry entry
# 'crk-master-corpus' in arena/datasets/registry.json).
crk-translate/eval/datasets/master_corpus.json
crk-translate/eval/datasets/split_metadata.json
crk-translate/eval/datasets/development/*.json
crk-translate/eval/datasets/held_out/*.json
crk-translate/eval/datasets/curated/*.json
# Quarantined contaminated sets (see quarantine/README.md — tracked)
crk-translate/eval/datasets/curated/quarantine/*.json

# ── Wolvengrey-derived dictionary data: NO redistribution ─────────
# arena/mt_eval_harness/eval_standards/crk/data/lemmas.json is a 5.2 MB
# lemma dictionary harvested from the itwêwina API (CW = Arok
# Wolvengrey's "nêhiyawêwin: itwêwina / Cree: Words", + MD).
# Redistribution permission is PENDING (docs/LICENSING.md) — it must
# never be tracked, subtree-pushed, or packaged. Found in the public
# gds-mt-eval-harness mirror on 2026-06-12 (security review); untracked
# here, and the mirror history must be purged before any re-push.
# The semantic validator reads it from disk locally; re-harvest with
# crk-translate tooling if missing.
arena/mt_eval_harness/eval_standards/crk/data/lemmas.json
.vercel

# Generated per-source split registries. build_registry.py writes these from
# the corpora cards (cli/shared/corpora-cards/). The merged registry.json IS
# tracked as the runtime registry; the split files are rebuilt on demand —
# and registry-flores.json alone is ~49 MB — so they must not be committed.
# (load_registry / generate_sweep_queue regenerate or fall back to them.)
arena/datasets/registry-*.json

# Bundled-in-the-wheel registry copy. build_registry.py generates it from the
# tracked arena/datasets/registry.json so `pip install` ships a registry; it is
# included in the wheel via package-data at build time, never committed.
arena/mt_eval_harness/data/registry.json

# ── Fetched/built corpus CONTENT — NEVER tracked (dataset doctrine) ────────
# The harness is fetch-from-source: every corpus is rebuilt at run time from
# its third-party upstream via the corpora-card recipe
# (cli/shared/corpora-cards/<card>.json -> source.repo_url + source.builder),
# cached under arena/datasets/.cache/, and sha-verified. ONLY the metadata
# cards and the merged registry.json are tracked — the actual parallel-text
# corpus files are third-party content and must never enter git or be hosted
# by us. (CLAUDE.md "Dataset doctrine". The quarantine gate enforces the
# crk/EdTeKLA subset; these rules keep ALL corpora out of the tree.)
#
# De-hosting migration COMPLETE (2026-06-22): the previously-tracked curated
# corpora were `git rm --cached`-ed and removed from git (kept on disk). The
# runnable queue curls ZERO of them — all 44 were quarantined catalogue
# entries — and the leaderboard's per-entry data lives in Supabase
# (run_card_entries), written at publish time from freshly-fetched corpora, so
# git never needs corpus content. These rules keep curated content out for good.
arena/datasets/curated/
# Loose corpus files dropped into a checkout by `curl -O` queue run_commands.
/arena/*-dev-v1.json
/arena/*-dev-v*.json
/arena/*-test-v1.json
/arena/*-test-v*.json

# ── Eval run artifacts (RunLogs + TestReports) — regenerated, never tracked ─
# `mt-eval run` writes run_<ts>.json + _report.json here; the leaderboard AND
# the homepage viz build from Supabase (the system of record), not from these
# files (founder directive 2026-06-16). Report JSONs are no longer tracked. The
# finer-grained rules live in arena/.gitignore (`eval/logs/*`, with only
# !sweep_manifest.json re-included) — NOT repeated here, because a root-level
# dir ignore (`arena/eval/logs/`) would block that re-include (git can't
# un-ignore a file whose parent directory is excluded).

# ── BLANKET no-corpus-content (repo-wide de-hosting, 2026-06-22) ────────────
# Champollion never hosts corpus CONTENT (translation pairs / parallel text /
# reference answers / eval gold) in git — ANY license, ANYWHERE. Corpora are
# fetch-from-source; only metadata cards + builders are tracked. The enforcing
# gate is scripts/quarantine_gate.sh (which runs scripts/corpus_content_scan.py,
# the license-agnostic content detector). These path rules de-host the specific
# trees that were untracked in the 2026-06-22 purge and stop them re-entering;
# the per-dir .gitignores (crk-translate/, cli/test/benchmark/) carry the same.
#
# Deprecated CLI translation benchmark — scraped third-party website text
# (content-bench/) and Signal Desktop UI strings (ui-bench/). Regenerated by the
# scrape/extract scripts; see cli/test/benchmark/DEPRECATED.md.
cli/test/benchmark/content-bench/raw/
cli/test/benchmark/content-bench/source/
cli/test/benchmark/content-bench/reference/
cli/test/benchmark/ui-bench/source/
cli/test/benchmark/ui-bench/reference/
#
# crk-translate eval corpus content — English->Plains-Cree pairs, references,
# and itwêwina/Wolvengrey-derived glossaries (redistribution not permitted).
crk-translate/eval/baseline_evals/results/
crk-translate/eval/baselines/raw_llm/
crk-translate/eval/baseline_results.json
crk-translate/eval/eval_results.json
crk-translate/eval/exports/termbank_*.json
crk-translate/eval/exports/termbank_*.csv
crk-translate/eval/baseline_evals/prompt_iterations/v6_phrasebook.json
crk-translate/eval/baseline_evals/prompt_iterations/v6_phrasebook.txt
crk-translate/eval/baseline_evals/prompt_iterations/v6_dictionary.txt
crk-translate/eval/baseline_evals/prompt_iterations/v7_lemma_list.txt
crk-translate/crk_translate/grammar/examples.json

# readme-i18n: docs/README.en.md is build input generated from cli/README.md by
# cli/scripts/build-readme-i18n-source.mjs — only the translated outputs are tracked.
cli/docs/README.en.md
local-assets/

# Champollion translation memory — LOCAL CACHE, never tracked (see
# cli/website/docs/concepts/translation-memory.md §"Should You Commit
# .champollion/tm.json?" and guides/agent-guide.md §Generated Files, which have
# said so all along). Untracked 2026-08-17; `champollion sync` repopulates it.
# The sibling lock files (.champollion.lock, .champollion-content.lock) STAY
# tracked — this rule matches only the directory.
.champollion/

# Site-docent grounding artifacts — BUILD OUTPUT, never tracked. Both files are
# emitted by cli/scripts/build-docent-corpus.mjs from the public docs tree
# (cli/website/docs) plus the tracked SSOTs in cli/shared/docent/
# (system-prompt.md, register-blocks.json, faq.en.json). They are ~1.8 MB each of
# flattened doc prose, and the sovereignty gate blocks both on sight
# (scripts/quarantine_gate.sh → "monolingual text records"): the corpus-content
# rule is deliberately blunt and license-agnostic, and it is not weakened for our
# own prose. Regenerate, don't commit — and note that the docent handler STATIC-
# imports the bundle, so a missing bundle fails the deploy loudly (TS2307) rather
# than shipping an ungrounded docent. Rebuild before deploying:
#   node cli/scripts/build-docent-corpus.mjs
cli/shared/docent/corpus.json
mt-eval-arena/supabase/functions/docent-chat/_generated/

# Audit findings — WORKING ARTIFACTS, never tracked. scripts/audit_runner.py
# emits ~1.8 MB of JSON per run (one timestamped snapshot + latest.json); a
# tracked copy would add that much history on every audit while being fully
# regenerable in one command:
#   python3 scripts/audit_runner.py --profile deep --report
# The DURABLE records are tracked and small: the ratchet baseline
# (cli/shared/card-lint-baseline.json, shrink-only) and the human report
# docs/audit/DATA_ACCURACY_AUDIT_<date>.md.
docs/audit/findings/

# Microsoft Office lock files. Word/PowerPoint drop a "~$name.pptx" stub
# beside any open document; it is a transient owner record, not content, and
# it appears untracked every time a deck is edited.
~$*
